Unknown option: --no-such-option

Usage:
    ingest-movies [options] <movieDir>...

    movieDir      directory holding the movies to ingest. Several may be given:
                  each is worked through in full, one after the other, in the
                  order they were typed. With tagging each gets lists of its own,
                  named after it.

    Options
    -------
    -f, --fragments <file>
                  read the name fragments to remove from <file> (one per line,
                  '#' comments and blank lines ignored). Default:
                  data/fragments.txt in the medialib data directory when it is
                  there, else no fragment removal.
    -r, --convert-remuxes
                  also convert the remuxes, last of all, with convert-video -k,
                  writing each converted copy beside its film as its AV1
                  edition. The film itself is left as it is. A full ingest
                  only.
    -k, --keep [part]
                  keep <part>, taking nothing away: audio (lossless audio stays
                  lossless), tracks (no track is dropped) and dv (a dual-layer
                  Dolby Vision profile 7 keeps its enhancement layer),
                  comma-separated; a bare -k keeps all three. Cannot be
                  combined with -r.
    -o, --omit [phase]
                  omit <phase> from a full ingest: junk, subtitles, ocr,
                  roles, commentary, chapters, plex and tagging,
                  comma-separated; a bare -o omits all eight.
    -O, --only <phases>
                  do only these phases, each on its own, over the whole tree
                  below each folder given, in the order typed and stopping at
                  the first that fails: layout, roles, ocr, tagging,
                  subtitles, commentary, names, chapters, extras-chapters,
                  plex and backups, comma-separated. Cannot be combined with
                  -r, -C, -k or -o.
    -C, --extras-chapters
                  also chapter the extras that have no chapters, by the
                  language model (docs/models.md). A full ingest
                  only.
    -P, --prompt <text>
                  with -C or -O extras-chapters: more instructions for the
                  model, added to every request.
    -w, --write   with -O tagging, subtitles, names or backups: carry out what
                  their dry run only prints. On its own it is refused.
    -i, --ids <file>
                  with -O tagging: the unmatched list, filled in with ids, read
                  back. A dry run unless -w is given.
    -v, --verbose Also say why each item was handled the way it was, and on a
                  failure print the tool's whole output rather than its last
                  lines.
    -q, --quiet   Print errors only - no progress and no warnings.
    -x, --set <name=value>
                  Override a setting for this run, over the settings file;
                  repeatable. A secret is refused - the settings file is where
                  it goes. The settings page lists the names.

    Phases
    ------
    A full ingest runs all but backups (and extras-chapters without -C), one
    level below each folder given, and remuxes each film once into an
    improved copy, keeping the original as "<name> (old).mkv". -O runs them
    one at a time over the whole tree.
    junk             deletes release junk (movieJunkExtensions) and samples
    layout           remuxes into Matroska, gives each film a folder, sorts the
                     extras and cleans the names
    roles            puts the subtitles' forced and SDH flags right
    ocr              reads picture subtitles into text (seconv)
    tagging          writes the IMDb id and editions into the names (tmdbApiKey)
    subtitles        downloads, syncs and tests the subtitles spokenLanguages
                     names
    commentary       finds and transcribes the commentary tracks (whisper)
    names            names numbered commentaries after who speaks in them
    chapters         gives the films their disc's chapters from ChapterDB
    extras-chapters  chapters the extras by the language model (-C)
    plex             compares each film with the Plex library's copy, and
                     carries over what it lacks
    backups          drops the (old) originals whose copies pass the checks

    Dependencies
    ------------
    Required: ffmpeg, mkvtoolnix, mediainfo. The optional tools, and what a
    run does without each, are in docs/requirements.md.

    Everything else: docs/commands/ingest-movies.md

Nothing was changed.
